  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Homeland Security obligated $60.3B in contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The Department of Homeland Security recorded 25,082 awards with an average award size of $2.4M, and obligations were up 112.7% year over year. Obligations by fiscal year show the Department of Homeland Security at $19.7B in FY21, $20.8B in FY22, $23.9B in FY23, $23.6B in FY24, $28.3B in FY25, and $60.3B in FY26. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction is the largest industry by obligations at $28.5B, followed by Ship Building and Repairing at $7.8B and Security Guards and Patrol Services at $3.6B. FISHER SAND & GRAVEL CO is the largest vendor by obligations at $13.4B, followed by BARNARD CONSTRUCTION COMPANY, INCORPORATED at $4.5B and DAVIE DEFENSE INC. at $3.5B. The top ten NAICS categories and the top ten vendors together show concentration in construction, shipbuilding, and security services across FY2026 to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has DHS contract spending changed year over year?",
        "body": "The Department of Homeland Security obligated $60.3B in FY2026 to date, and obligations were up 112.7% year over year. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $19.7B in FY21, $20.8B in FY22, $23.9B in FY23, $23.6B in FY24, and $28.3B in FY25, showing the fiscal trajectory through FY26. The count of awards for FY2026 to date is 25,082 with an average award size of $2.4M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which industries and vendors dominate DHS contracts?",
        "body": "Commercial and Institutional Building Construction is the largest NAICS category at $28.5B, followed by Ship Building and Repairing at $7.8B and Security Guards and Patrol Services at $3.6B. FISHER SAND & GRAVEL CO is the largest vendor at $13.4B, followed by BARNARD CONSTRUCTION COMPANY, INCORPORATED at $4.5B and DAVIE DEFENSE INC. at $3.5B. The list of top categories and vendors highlights heavy obligations in construction, shipbuilding, and security-related services."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of Homeland Security spend on contracts?",
      "a": "Department of Homeland Security obligated $60.3B on contracts in FY2026 to date. The Department of Homeland Security recorded 25,082 awards with an average award size of $2.4M, and obligations were up 112.7% year over year. Historical obligations were $19.7B in FY21, $20.8B in FY22, $23.9B in FY23, $23.6B in FY24, and $28.3B in FY25."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Homeland Security buy?",
      "a": "The Department of Homeland Security buys large amounts of construction, shipbuilding, and security services. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction accounts for $28.5B, Ship Building and Repairing accounts for $7.8B, and Security Guards and Patrol Services accounts for $3.6B, with other categories including consulting, computer services, and engineering."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are Homeland Security's largest contractors?",
      "a": "FISHER SAND & GRAVEL CO is the largest contractor for the Department of Homeland Security at $13.4B. Other top contractors are BARNARD CONSTRUCTION COMPANY, INCORPORATED at $4.5B, DAVIE DEFENSE INC. at $3.5B, SLS FEDERAL SERVICES LLC at $2.4B, and SPENCER CONSTRUCTION LLC at $2.4B, with additional top vendors listed through $1.1B."
